      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "FOOT FALCON (4) was out of the placings last time but shapes well for this on his blistering win the start prior, getting around Northam over 509m in 29.46. Has the ability and looks hard to top. AGASSI (2) copped a check in the run last time but wound up strongly to hit the frame when third (28.20) in a Grade 4/5 at this track. This tougher but looks a leading chance again. MY MUM MIA (7) has a strong record this journey here with two wins and a minor from five starts. Comes off a (27.89) win last time, scoring by half a length in a Novice race over 488m at this track. Among the main chances. MALCOLM BYTE (1) should be thereabouts despite an unplaced run here most recently.",
